+# Recovery directory mechanics: isolated source model
+
+The runner compiles the actual `recovery-directory-handles.cpp` against the
+small Win32 declarations and object model in this directory. The model is a
+test boundary, not a production scope issuer. It never loads the native
+module into an application, connects to PostgreSQL, changes an installed
+directory, or supplies authentication or backup/restore evidence.
+
+Unlike a flag-recording stub, its file opens enforce share conflicts in both
+directions. Paths name model objects; separate handles retain the same original
+object. Independent rename and reparse attempts consult live opens, rather than
+calling the implementation's recheck. Relative exclusive creation is resolved
+through the supplied original parent handle and returns the new child handle
+in the same operation. Collisions preserve the original contents.
+
+Every result says `SYNTHETIC_NATIVE_MECHANICS`, Windows execution `NOT_RUN`, and
+physical authority `false`. A successful mechanical test cannot replace either
+existing JavaScript HOLD fence or qualify Windows sharing, process lifetime,
+ACLs, kernel calls, physical recovery or production authority.
+
+The 34 cases run in fresh executable processes. They cover complete ancestry,
+sharing in both directions, post-check namespace swaps, retained anchors and
+attribute-only reparse attempts, same-object comparisons despite equal IDs,
+exclusive relative creation and collision preservation, unanchored-child
+refusal, cancellation and late completion, exact callback tickets, original
+worker/Job joins, partial transfer and handle reuse. Allocation failures after
+creation and during transfer verification are injected by the modeled native
+boundary; the actual C++ exception paths must retain originals and avoid
+deadlock. Independent mutation controls succeed after a confirmed release.
+
+The crash case checks directory and anchor copies in the one registered
+process's separate handle table after the modeled holder dies. It does not
+prove that unregistered descendants received copies, that an authenticated
+runner bound every worker before resume, or that a helper owns the original
+Job across a real crash. Those integrations remain absent and cannot be
+replaced with this model, a diagnostic binding record, or a successful ticket.
+
+Run from `apps/metaengine-browser`:
+
+```sh
+node --test test/recovery-directory-handles.test.mjs
+```
